 35CL    34S(P,P),(P,P'G):RESONANCES   1967KO19,1977OU01,1981BI05ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL c  {+34}S(p,p'|g) measurements:                                           
 35CL c  1967Ko19: E=2.78-3.08-MeV proton beams were produced from the 4-MeV    
 35CL2c  electrostatic accelerator of the Physical-Technical Institute of the   
 35CL3c  Ukrainian SSR Academy of Sciences, in energy step of 1 keV. Target was 
 35CL4c  enriched thin {+34}S. |g rays were detected with a 70 by 60 mm NaI(Tl) 
 35CL5c  crystal for detecting the 2.13 MeV |g-ray of {+34}S decay, resolution  
 35CL6c  of 11.5% for the 0.622 MeV {+137}Cs line. Measured |s(E{-p},|q) from   
 35CL7c  yields of the 2.13 MeV |g-ray, p|g(|q) of the 2.13 MeV |g-ray. Deduced 
 35CL8c  resonance energies, J, |p, relative resonance intensities.             
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  {+34}S(p,p) measurement:                                               
 35CL c  1977Ou01: E=1.45-2.82 MeV proton beams were produced from the TUNL 3-MV
 35CL2c  Van de Graaff accelerator in energy steps of 100 eV for on-resonance   
 35CL3c  and 400 eV for off-resonance, overall FWHM=350-450 eV. Target was CdS  
 35CL4c  90% enriched {+34}S evaporated onto 5-10 |mg/cm{+2} carbon backings.   
 35CL5c  Scattered protons were detected with surface barrier detectors at 90|',
 35CL6c  105|', 135|' and 160|'. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced resonance       
 35CL7c  energies, J, |p, |G{-p} from R-Matrix analysis.                        
 35CL c  1981Bi05: E=1.4-2.8 MeV proton beams were produced from the Groningen 5
 35CL2c  MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were 4 and 1 |mg/cm{+2}          
 35CL3c  Sb{-2}S{-3} (90% in {+34}S) evaporated onto 10 |mg/cm{+2} carbon       
 35CL4c  backings. Scattered protons were detected with three silicon surface   
 35CL5c  barrier detectors at 88|', 124|' and 174|'. Measured |s(E{-p},|q).     
 35CL6c  Deduced resonance energies, J, |p, |G{-p}. Also measured (p,|g).       
 35CL c  1971BrXT: Measured |s(E{-p}). Deduced resonance energies, J, |p,       
 35CL2c  widths.                                                                
 35CL c  1974Bi16: E=1.2-2.1 MeV protons were produced from the Helsinki        
 35CL2c  University 2.5 MV van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were prepared from
 35CL3c  natural sulphur (4.22% {+34}S) with {+34}S ions embedded into carbon   
 35CL4c  foils. Scattered protons were detected with four silicon surface       
 35CL5c  barrier detectors. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced resonance energies,  
 35CL6c  J, |p, widths from analysis of the resonances.                         
 35CL c  Others: 1978Ce02, 1980Fa07, 1983Ch50, 1988Za04, 2019Ka53.              
 35CL cL $A{-2} and A{-4} values under comments are from p|g(|q) of the 2.13 MeV
 35CL2cL |g-ray from {+34}S (1967Ko19)                                          
 35CL cL $I(res) under comments are resonance intensities relative to 1 for     
 35CL2cL E{-p}(lab)=2799 resonance (1967Ko19).                                  
 35CL cL E$From E(level)=E{-p}(cm)+S(p)({+35}Cl), where S(p)=6370.81 {I4}       
 35CL2cL (2021Wa16) and E{-p}(cm) deduced from E{-p}(lab) by                    
 35CL3cL E{-p}(cm)=E{-p}(lab)*[m({+34}S)/(m({+34}S)+m(p))].                     
 35CL cL J$From comparison of experimental differential cross sections with     
 35CL2cL theoretical predictions by R-Matrix calculations (1977Ou01) for levels 
 35CL3cL up to 9101 level and from p|g(|q) (1967Ko19) for levels after that.    
 35CL cL T,S$From 1977Ou01 up to 9101 level and from 1967Ko19 after that, unless
 35CL2cL otherwise noted. 1977Ou01 state that although the absolute proton      
 35CL3cL energies are accurate only to about 3 keV, the relative values of      
 35CL4cL E{-p}(lab) should be reliable to within a few hundred eV, based on     
 35CL5cL which the evaluators have assigned a 0.5 keV uncertainty for E{-p}(lab)
 35CL6cL and 3 keV uncertainty for E(level) from 1977Ou01                       
